        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(android): bind app chat to a dedicated session",
        "body": "Related: #45854\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where Android app chat could reuse the gateway's generic main session context after pairing, so app-originated chat history and follow-up requests were not cleanly isolated from other OpenClaw surfaces connected to the same agent.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Android app now derives a stable `openclaw-app-*` session key for each connected gateway endpoint, explicitly creates that app session after a successful operator connection, and binds chat/history/talk mode to that key before app chat traffic resumes.\n\nThe app session create request intentionally omits parent-session and emit-hook fields, so the Android app session is independent rather than a child of another surface. The proof workflow is manual-only behind `workflow_dispatch` + `include_android`, so normal push/PR CI does not run the emulator media capture by default.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAndroid app users get a dedicated OpenClaw App session per gateway connection. Reconnects and gateway switches keep app chat scoped to the Android app's session instead of blending into the agent's default `main` chat or other connected surfaces.\n\n## Evidence\n\nGitHub Actions on `snowzlmbot/openclaw`, exact head SHA `838fa5dde4aec11e1f575c6092f95127ea81959f`:\n\n- Full CI run passed: https://github.com/snowzlmbot/openclaw/actions/runs/28907001143\n- Android app session media proof job passed: https://github.com/snowzlmbot/openclaw/actions/runs/28907001143/job/85758758496\n- Media/log artifact: https://github.com/snowzlmbot/openclaw/actions/runs/28907001143/artifacts/8154958242\n\nThe artifact contains:\n\n- `openclaw-app-session-proof.mp4` and `openclaw-app-session-proof.png` from a real Android emulator run.\n- `session-create.json` showing the app created `agent:main:openclaw-app-1f52fae09049` with label `OpenClaw App · Proof Pixel`.\n- `gateway-events.jsonl` showing `sessions.create` followed by `chat.history` using the same app session key.\n- `logcat-tail.txt` and the debug APK used for the emulator proof.\n\nRelevant captured `sessions.create` payload:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"method\": \"sessions.create\",\n  \"key\": \"agent:main:openclaw-app-1f52fae09049\",\n  \"label\": \"OpenClaw App · Proof Pixel\",\n  \"agentId\": \"main\",\n  \"hasParentSessionKey\": false,\n  \"hasEmitCommandHooks\": false\n}\n```\n\nLocal lightweight checks run before pushing:\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `ruby -e \"require 'yaml'; YAML.load_file('.github/workflows/ci.yml', aliases: true); puts 'ci yaml ok'\"`\n- `pnpm native:i18n:check`\n\n## Evidence Source Map\n\n- Dedicated Android app session key: `session-create.json` from the media proof artifact.\n- App chat binding to the dedicated session: `gateway-events.jsonl` shows `chat.history` with the same `agent:main:openclaw-app-*` key.\n- No child-session coupling: `session-create.json` records `hasParentSessionKey: false` and `hasEmitCommandHooks: false`.\n- Real UI/media evidence: emulator screenshot and MP4 in the uploaded artifact.\n- CI coverage: successful run `28907001143` at the exact PR head SHA.\n\n## Risk\n\n- Low runtime risk: the session key is derived from the gateway endpoint/device identity and remains stable across reconnects.\n- The change touches Android session binding and chat history routing; tests cover key generation and chat controller session policy.\n- The emulator proof job is manual-only and pinned to full action SHAs.\n\n## Rollback\n\nRevert this PR to return Android chat to the previous gateway main-session behavior and remove the manual emulator proof job.\n\n## Docs Updated\n\n- `apps/android/README.md` documents the dedicated `OpenClaw App · <device>` session behavior.\n- `apps/.i18n/native-source.json` was synced after Android source changes.\n",
